0..77 Comment "// Two programs exchange a ping over `Net`, the host interface for streams to"
78..107 Comment "// peers named by their keys."
108..110 Comment "//"
111..186 Comment "// One process serves and another pings it, the first step from one process"
187..260 Comment "// to programs that coordinate across hosts. The same `ping` runs under a"
261..318 Comment "// handler written here, a second model of the interface."
319..321 Comment "//"
322..398 Comment "// `gandr run ping.gandr` serves, and `gandr run ping.gandr <key>@<ip:port>`"
399..472 Comment "// dials the server that key and socket name, then prints its answer. The"
473..548 Comment "// host binds its network on the run\'s first `Net` operation, at the socket"
549..611 Comment "// `--net-bind` names, under the key `GANDR_NET_SECRET` holds."
612..614 Comment "//"
615..683 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
684..755 Comment "// - see: `crates/runtime-net/README.md` — the network the host binds"
757..832 Comment "/// Accept one stream, read its ping, answer `pong`, disconnect, and return"
833..846 Comment "/// the ping."
